      "isPinned": false,
      "content": "I have some questions about how chiplets and multi - die manufacturing works:-\n\n1. What process node is used for the parts connecting the dies (if both die are from different foundries, one of them has to do the job of connecting everything?)\n2. Do any of the open source tools have a concept of instantiating a design with multiple PDKs in different partitions + interconnects between them?\n3. Are all dies usually from different foundries or just different processes from same foundry and are there companies that just do interposer / wiring connection before packaging for this type of stuff?",
